-- Queries logical processors and temporarily pins the calling thread.
public define placement as opaque.
-- Number of online logical processors in the host system.
public use "topology" function count giving failable unsigned.
-- CPUs available to this calling thread (within its Windows processor group).
public use "topology" function allowed giving failable unsigned.
-- OS logical processor identifier for the calling thread.
public use "topology" function current giving failable unsigned.
-- NUMA discovery is available on Windows and Linux. CPU IDs match current/pin.
public use "topology" function nodes giving failable unsigned.
public use "topology" function node(cpu unsigned) giving failable unsigned.
-- Pins this thread to an available CPU in the requested NUMA node.
public use "topology" function place(node unsigned) giving failable pointer to placement.
-- Pins this thread to one online logical processor and saves its prior affinity.
public use "topology" function pin(cpu unsigned) giving failable pointer to placement.
-- Restores the affinity saved by pin. Call from the same thread, once.
public use "topology" function restore(value pointer to placement) giving failable nothing.
